>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Site-by-site g-xTB correction of ligand connectivity. The original CSD phosphorus-containing three-membered ring and P–PPh₃ skeleton both match the input. The two ring P–C distances are 1.816 and 1.810 Å, Their bond orders are 0.974 and 0.981. Retain the four-coordinate terminal phosphonium P⁺, Restore neutral formal charges on C and P at the ring closure, Assign W(0) to the tungsten pentacarbonyl, Total charge +1. Localized 30 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths. Use the supplied Lewis representation for scoring; Independent evidence for the complete graph is limited.

>  <UPSTREAM_COMPARISON>
Not equivalent

>  <SPIN_REVIEW>
Not independently verified

